course: dictionary
lesson: 15562
title: Words for the beach
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A surfboard is a long, narrow board. You stand or lie on it to ride the waves in the sea. Surf means riding waves, so a surfboard is a board for surfing. The word is made of two smaller words: surf and board.
explain: «Mia paddled out on her surfboard, past the breaking waves.» Paddled means moved with her arms while lying on the board. The clues are the sea and the waves, so a surfboard must be a board you use in the water.
explain: «Dad waxed his surfboard so his feet would not slip.» Wax is put on the top of the board to stop your feet slipping. Try your meaning in the sentence: if a surfboard is a board for riding waves, the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A surfboard is a long, narrow board for riding waves in the sea.
fact: «Surfboards» is the plural, so you can have one surfboard or two surfboards.
fact: Phrases you may hear are «ride a surfboard», «wax a surfboard» and «a surfboard leash».
fact: A surfboard leash is a cord that keeps the board close to you in the water.
fact: Surf between the flags, with a lifeguard, and always keep hold of your board.
exercise: «Mia paddled out on her surfboard, past the breaking waves.» Where did Mia go on her surfboard? | Into the shop | Up a mountain | Back to the car park | *Out past the waves in the sea
exercise: What is a surfboard? | *A long, narrow board for riding waves | A small boat with a sail | A bed for lying on the sand | A wide raft for the swimming pool
exercise: «Dad waxed his surfboard so his feet would not slip.» Why did Dad wax his surfboard? | To wash the sand off | To paint it a new colour | To make it heavier | *So his feet would not slip
test: «Always surf between the flags, with a lifeguard, and keep hold of your surfboard.» What should you do with your surfboard? | Leave it on the sand | Hide it under a towel | Throw it to a friend | *Keep hold of it
test: Surfboard is a compound word, made of two smaller words joined together. Which two words make it? | sun and bed | sea and sand | wave and boat | *surf and board
exam: «Ruby rode her surfboard in Cornwall, then sat on the sand to dry off.» Where did Ruby ride her surfboard? | In a shop window | On a mountain, far from water | In a park with a swing | *In the sea, at Cornwall
